    "note": "Constitutional monarchy with strong princely powers: the Prince can veto laws (a 2012 referendum to curtail the veto over referendum results was rejected) and the 2003 referendum approved the 'Princely Initiative' constitution. The government is led by the Head of Government (Regierungschef). Hereditary Prince Alois has exercised the Prince's powers as regent since 15 August 2004 while Hans-Adam II remains head of state. Laws can be put to referendum by popular initiative (1,000 signatures for legislative initiatives)."
